@node SCUMM Lexical Elements
@section Lexical Elements

@subsection Keywords

SCUMM reserves the following keywords (case-insensitive):

@table @code
@item action, actor
Actor and action declaration
@item breakhere
Debugger breakpoint
@item class
Class definition
@item const
Constant definition
@item do, end
Block delimiters
@item else, elseif
Conditional constructs
@item enum
Enumeration type
@item fadeIn, fadeOut
Visual effects
@item for, in, to
Iteration construct
@item function
Function definition
@item if, then
Conditional
@item invariant
Class invariant assertion
@item local
Local variable declaration
@item method
Method definition
@item object
Game object declaration
@item override
Method override
@item private, public, protected
Access modifiers
@item property
Property declaration
@item return
Function return
@item script
Script/routine definition
@item self
Self reference
@item sound
Sound resource
@item variable
Global variable
@item verb
Verb definition
@item while, repeat, until
Loop constructs
@end table

@subsection Identifiers

Identifiers follow these rules:

@itemize
@item Case-insensitive
@item Start with letter or underscore
@item Contain letters, digits, underscores
@item Examples: @code{MainChar}, @code{room_10}, @code{_temp}
@end itemize

